    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Lists, Indexes, and Calculations\r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Ask AI Tutor to write a program that:\r\n\r\n   * Stores four item prices in a list\r\n   * Accesses two elements from the list using their indexes\r\n   * Uses an expression to add the two prices\r\n   * Builds and prints a message with the total\r\n\r\n2. Run the program and examine AI Tutor’s code.\r\n\r\n3. Use AI Tutor’s code as a model to create your own list-based calculation program. Choose what values your list will store and what your program will calculate.\r\n\r\n   Your program must:\r\n\r\n   * Store at least four elements in a list\r\n   * Access at least two elements using their indexes\r\n   * Use the elements in an expression\r\n   * Store the result in a variable\r\n   * Build and print a message that includes the result\r\n\r\n   Your list could store prices, distances, scores, times, measurements, or other numeric data you choose.\r\n\r\n4. Run your program and fix any errors. You may ask AI Tutor for hints, but do not ask it to write your program for you.",
